{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Save</b> — Since he mentioned that HaShem was his strength and his heart exulted, he prayed that He would shepherd Israel; therefore: 'Save and bless,' to add HaShem upon them and guard them like a shepherd; therefore: 'and shepherd them and bear them,' meaning that they dwell in a high place where beasts cannot harm them. And Rabbi Moses said: that 'and bear them' means He will provide their needs, in the manner that the people of his place bear him up [support him]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:48.758495127Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}